@module flutter-m20 | Advanced Professional Development
@summary Flutter internals, native interop, background work, sync, modular and large-scale design, multi-platform delivery.

@lesson flutter-m20-l01 | Advanced Dart patterns | 8
## Learning objectives
- Use modern Dart idioms in large codebases

## Advanced Dart patterns
Sealed classes for states, records for lightweight results, extension types for IDs, and pattern matching for exhaustive UI logic.

```dart
extension type LessonId(String value) {}
sealed class Load<T> {}
class Ready<T> extends Load<T> { Ready(this.data); final T data; }
class Failed<T> extends Load<T> {}
```

## Summary
- Let the type system prevent bugs.

@lesson flutter-m20-l02 | Flutter internals | 8
## Learning objectives
- Understand elements and render objects

## Flutter internals
Widgets configure Elements, which manage RenderObjects. `canUpdate` (same runtimeType and key) decides whether an element is reused; keys control identity.

```dart
import 'package:flutter/widgets.dart';

bool reusable(Widget a, Widget b) => Widget.canUpdate(a, b);
```

## Summary
- Keys and types decide element reuse.

@lesson flutter-m20-l03 | Native interoperability | 8
## Learning objectives
- Go beyond platform channels

## Native interoperability
Pigeon generates type-safe channel code; dart:ffi calls C libraries directly; jnigen and ffigen generate bindings for Java/Kotlin and Objective-C/Swift.

```dart
// dart run pigeon --input pigeons/messages.dart
void main() {}
```

## Summary
- Prefer generated, type-safe bindings.

@lesson flutter-m20-l04 | Background tasks | 8
## Learning objectives
- Run work when the app isn't open

## Background tasks
Use `workmanager` for deferrable periodic tasks on Android/iOS, and respect OS limits on background execution.

```dart
// Workmanager().registerPeriodicTask('sync', 'syncTask', frequency: const Duration(hours: 6));
void main() {}
```

## Summary
- Background work is limited by the OS.

@lesson flutter-m20-l05 | Offline synchronization | 8
## Learning objectives
- Sync local changes reliably

## Offline synchronization
Queue offline changes with IDs and timestamps, sync when online, and resolve conflicts (last-write-wins or merge).

```dart
class PendingChange { PendingChange(this.id, this.payload, this.updatedAt); final String id; final Map<String, Object?> payload; final DateTime updatedAt; }
```

## Summary
- Queue, retry and resolve conflicts.

@lesson flutter-m20-l06 | Modular architecture | 8
## Learning objectives
- Split large apps into packages

## Modular architecture
Use a monorepo with local packages per feature and tools such as Melos or Dart pub workspaces to manage them.

```dart
// pubspec.yaml (workspace root)
// workspace:
//   - packages/core
//   - packages/feature_lessons
void main() {}
```

## Summary
- Packages enforce boundaries.

